Package: proxlb-pve
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: credativ GmbH <support@credativ.de>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: perl, libjson-perl, pve-manager
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/credativ/ProxLB
Description: ProxLB for Proxmox VE - LXC installer and web-interface plugin
 Deploys ProxLB, the load balancer and resource scheduler for Proxmox VE
 clusters, in its own highly available LXC container (proxlb-lxc), and adds
 a "Datacenter -> ProxLB" tab to the Proxmox VE web interface showing node
 usage, the balance spread and planned or performed migrations, with
 buttons for a dry-run preview, a rebalance and automatic balancing.
 .
 For ProxLB running on another machine, proxlb-external connects it to
 the same tab through a small anchor VM.
 .
 The ProxLB source is bundled, so the container can be created without git
 on the host. A dpkg trigger re-applies the web-interface plugin after
 pve-manager updates. Install this package on every node whose web
 interface you use.
